export default "import { Meta } from '@storybook/addon-docs/blocks';\n\n<Meta title=\"Docs/Storybook Column Modules Documentation\" />\n\n# Storybook Column Modules Documentation\n\n## Overview\nThis document summarizes the evolution of our Storybook architecture to feature the three primary column components from our application as separate, top-level modules. The restructuring organizes our design system around the core functional areas of the AI workspace.\n\n## What Was Accomplished\n\n### 1. Analysis of Application Structure\n- Reviewed the `WritingAreaIndex.tsx` component to understand the three-column layout\n- Identified the actual components that make up each column in the live application:\n  - **Left Column**: `ResponsivePromptBuilderWithDnD` (Permanent - Prompt construction interface)\n  - **Right Column**: `InteractiveChatInterface` (Permanent - Trace, variables, tools, and data views)\n  - **Third Column**: Dynamic column that can load various content modules (A/B testing, Writing Area, etc.)\n\n### 2. Created Module Directories with Correct Architecture\nDirectories were created under `frontend/src/storybook/modules/` with the following structure:\n\n#### Featured Modules (Permanent Columns)\nThese columns are always present in the application:\n\n##### LeftColumn (`/modules/LeftColumn/`)\n- **Purpose**: Permanent Prompt Builder interface\n- **Key Component**: `ResponsivePromptBuilderWithDnD`\n- **Stories Included**:\n  - `Default`: Full component with drag-and-drop functionality\n  - `WithoutDnD`: Fallback version without drag-and-drop\n  - `ContextAwarePromptBuilder`: Configurable version with args\n  - `DesignSystemExamples`: Documentation of component features\n\n##### RightColumn (`/modules/RightColumn/`)\n- **Purpose**: Permanent Interactive Chat/Trace interface\n- **Key Component**: `InteractiveChatInterface`\n- **Stories Included**:\n  - `Default`: Full multi-tab interface\n  - `TraceView`: Execution trace visualization\n  - `VariablesView`: Variable history and A/B testing\n  - `ContextAwareChatInterface`: Configurable version with args\n  - `DesignSystemExamples`: Documentation of component features\n\n#### Dynamic Column Content (Third Column)\nThe third column is dynamic and can load different content modules:\n\n##### ThirdColumn (`/modules/ThirdColumn/`)\n- **Purpose**: A/B Testing Response Cards (one possible content for the third column)\n- **Key Component**: `ResponseCard` (multiple instances)\n- **Stories Included**:\n  - `Default`: Side-by-side response cards\n  - `CollapsedView`: Mixed expanded/collapsed state\n  - `SingleResponseCard`: Single card view\n  - `ContextAwareResponseCards`: Configurable version with args\n  - `DesignSystemExamples`: Documentation of component features\n\n##### WritingArea (`/modules/WritingArea/`)\n- **Purpose**: Writing interface (another possible content for the third column)\n- **Key Component**: `WritingArea`\n- **Stories Included**:\n  - `Default`: Full writing interface\n  - `ContextAwareWritingArea`: Configurable version\n  - `WithCustomContent`: Example with custom content\n  - `DesignSystemExamples`: Documentation of component features\n\n### 3. Design System Organization\nEach module directory follows a consistent pattern:\n1. **Default Story**: Shows the actual component in its natural environment\n2. **Variant Stories**: Different states and configurations\n3. **Context-Aware Stories**: Configurable versions with Storybook args\n4. **Design System Documentation**: Explains the component's purpose and features\n\n### 4. Preservation of Existing Structure\n- All existing files and directories were preserved\n- The existing `ProgramColumns` directory remains untouched\n- The new structure complements rather than replaces existing organization\n\n## Technical Implementation Details\n\n### File Structure\n```\nfrontend/src/storybook/modules/\n├── ColumnSystem/           # Existing - column layout components\n├── ProgramColumns/         # Existing - program column stories  \n├── LeftColumn/            # NEW - Prompt Builder module\n│   └── LeftColumn.stories.tsx\n├── RightColumn/           # NEW - Interactive Chat module\n│   └── RightColumn.stories.tsx\n├── ThirdColumn/           # NEW - A/B Testing module\n│   └── ThirdColumn.stories.tsx\n└── WritingArea/           # Existing - Writing Area module\n    └── WritingArea.stories.tsx\n```\n\n### Storybook Hierarchy\nThe new modules appear in Storybook under:\n```\nAI Workspace/\n├── Featured Modules/          # Permanent columns\n│   ├── Left Column\n│   └── Right Column  \n├── Dynamic Column/            # Third column content (interchangeable)\n│   ├── Third Column (A/B Testing)\n│   └── Writing Area\n└── Column Modules/            # Existing structure\n    └── Program Columns\n```\n\n### Key Features of Each Module\n\n#### Left Column (Prompt Builder)\n- Drag-and-drop prompt construction\n- Real-time preview\n- Context-aware suggestions\n- Modular component architecture\n\n#### Right Column (Interactive Chat)\n- Multi-tab interface (Trace, Variables, Tools, Data)\n- Execution trace visualization\n- Variable history and A/B testing\n- Tool registry and usage tracking\n- Approval queue for team submissions\n\n#### Third Column (A/B Testing)\n- Side-by-side response comparison\n- Expandable/collapsible cards\n- Model selection (GPT-4.1, Claude 3, etc.)\n- Technical diagram display\n- Publish/share/export functionality\n\n## Benefits of This Structure\n\n### 1. **Improved Discoverability**\n- Primary application features are now top-level modules\n- Clear separation of concerns between different functional areas\n- Easy navigation for developers and designers\n\n### 2. **Better Documentation**\n- Each module includes design system documentation\n- Context-aware stories demonstrate configurability\n- Clear explanation of each component's purpose\n\n### 3. **Enhanced Testing**\n- Isolated testing of each column component\n- Ability to test different states and configurations\n- Visual regression testing for each functional area\n\n### 4. **Scalability**\n- New modules can be added following the same pattern\n- Consistent structure makes maintenance easier\n- Clear boundaries between different application areas\n\n## How to Use the New Structure\n\n### For Developers\n1. **Find Components**: Navigate to the appropriate module directory\n2. **Understand Usage**: Review the design system examples\n3. **Test Variations**: Use context-aware stories to test different configurations\n4. **Add New Stories**: Follow the established pattern for consistency\n\n### For Designers\n1. **Review Components**: Access Storybook at `http://localhost:6006`\n2. **Explore Variations**: Use the controls panel to adjust component properties\n3. **Understand Context**: Read the design system documentation for each module\n4. **Provide Feedback**: Use Storybook's annotation features\n\n### For Product Managers\n1. **Visual Reference**: See all application features in one place\n2. **Feature Understanding**: Review the documentation for each module\n3. **Specification Reference**: Use stories as living documentation\n4. **Progress Tracking**: Monitor component development and testing\n\n## Next Steps\n\n### Short Term\n1. Add more context-aware stories for edge cases\n2. Improve documentation with more detailed examples\n3. Add accessibility testing for each module\n\n### Medium Term\n1. Create composite stories showing column interactions\n2. Add performance testing stories\n3. Create mobile-responsive variants\n\n### Long Term\n1. Expand to include all major application features\n2. Create cross-module integration stories\n3. Develop automated visual testing pipeline\n\n## Related Documentation\n\nFor more detailed information about specific aspects of our architecture:\n\n### The Magical Third Column\n- **Location**: `storybook/docs/MAGICAL_THIRD_COLUMN.md`\n- **Description**: Detailed vision document describing the Third Column as a massive, expandable AI output window that can load anything computable, with collapsible side panels and future-ready architecture.\n\n### Project Overview for Stakeholders\n- **Location**: `STORYBOOK_PROJECT_OVERVIEW.md`\n- **Description**: High-level overview suitable for hiring managers, investors, and non-technical stakeholders.\n\n### Architecture & Deployment\n- **Location**: `STORYBOOK_ARCHITECTURE_AND_DEPLOYMENT_SUMMARY.md`\n- **Description**: Technical details about Storybook architecture changes and deployment processes.\n\n## Conclusion\n\nThe restructuring of Storybook to feature the three column modules as top-level directories represents a significant improvement in our design system organization. By aligning our Storybook structure with the actual application architecture, we've created a more intuitive, maintainable, and scalable documentation system that better serves developers, designers, and product stakeholders.\n\nThe new structure makes it easy to:\n- Find and understand application components\n- Test different configurations and states\n- Document design decisions and patterns\n- Scale the system as the application grows\n\nThis evolution of our Storybook architecture provides a solid foundation for continued growth and improvement of our AI workspace application."